<!--
    GH-876 (kuna): "x86-64: a declared int passed to a variadic call in its
    own register prints as CONCAT44 of an uninitialized upper half"
    https://github.com/Noelo-Lab/kuna/issues/876

    Source:
      int pr(const char *f, ...);
      int d4(const char *f, int a) { pr(f, a); return pr(f, a); }
      int du(const char *f, unsigned a) { pr(f, a); return pr(f, a); }
      int d3(const char *f, int x, int a) { pr(f, x, a); return pr(f, x, a); }
      int dl(const char *f, long a) { pr(f, a + 1); return pr(f, a); }
      int c4(const char *f, int a) { pr(f, a); return pr(f, a); }
      int __attribute__((ms_abi)) mpr(const char *f, ...);
      int __attribute__((ms_abi)) w4(const char *f, int a)
        { mpr(f, a); return mpr(f, a); }
      int u5(const char *f, int a) { pr(f, a, a); return pr(f, a); }
      int u8(const char *f, int a, int b) { pr(f, a, b, a); return pr(f, b, a); }
      int c5(const char *f, int a) { pr(f, a, a); return pr(f, a); }

    d4, du, d3 and dl are gcc -O2, c4 is clang -O2, linked at 0x100000 with
    a `ret` standing in for pr at 0x1000e1.  w4 is gcc -O2 with the Windows
    x64 convention, linked at 0x100200 with mpr at 0x100226.  u5 and u8 are
    gcc -O2 and c5 is clang -O2, linked at 0x100300 calling the same pr.  The
    first call of each function passes each int in the register it arrived in
    (esi, plus edx in d3 and u8; edx in w4) while a copy is kept for the second
    call.  In u5, u8 and c5 the same int is also copied into a later argument
    register of that first call.

    Stage model: P4 call recovery, active-input-trial scoring.  The 8-byte
    register trial's value pieces the declared 4-byte input with the
    undeclared upper half of the register.  It is active, or, where the same
    value has a second reader in the call (u5, u8, c5), inactive and later
    gap-filled at 8 bytes; either way the call printed CONCAT44(v1,a) with v1
    never set.  `option varargforward` narrows such a trial to the int width
    when the upper bytes are only that undeclared register half.  dl passes a
    computed long, which stays 8 bytes.

    Pass 1 (`option varargforward off`) reproduces the bug: eight first calls
    print CONCAT44.  Pass 2 (default, on) prints pr(f,a), pr(f,x,a),
    mpr(f,a), pr(f,a,a), pr(f,a,b,a) and clang's pr(f,a,(uint8)(uint4)a).
-->
